# title: Globally floored cliquet
# category: Cliquets
# underlyings: 1
# source: Wilmott, Cliquet Options and Volatility Models, Wilmott Magazine, 2002
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: Twelve monthly returns, each clipped to a range, summed, with a guaranteed minimum on the total.
# param: notional = 1000 | amount | Notional
# param: local_floor = -0.03 | percent | Floor on each monthly return
# param: local_cap = 0.03 | percent | Cap on each monthly return
# param: global_floor = 0.02 | percent | Guaranteed minimum of the sum
#
# The global floor is what makes it sensitive to the forward smile.

2027-01-04
    notional = 1000
    local_floor = -0.03
    local_cap = 0.03
    global_floor = 0.02
    ref = spot()
    total = 0

schedule(2027-02-04, 2027-12-04, 1M, US, F)
    total = total + min(max(spot() / ref - 1, local_floor), local_cap)
    ref = spot()

2028-01-04
    total = total + min(max(spot() / ref - 1, local_floor), local_cap)
    pays notional * max(total, global_floor)
